  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 99bb79ad394217b4bb00b616185b7793, type: 3}
  m_Name: Ending_StayInValley
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Ending
  endingTitle: Valley
  titleDA: Bliver I Dalen
  descriptionDA: "Pandaen bliver i dalen, hvor skov og landsby m\xF8des. Der er bambus
    og vand nok til at klare sig, men der er ogs\xE5 st\xF8j, trafik og mennesker
    t\xE6t p\xE5. Hver ny forstyrrelse g\xF8r det sv\xE6rere at finde ro. \n\n \nI
    dalene konkurrerer mennesker og vilde dyr om pladsen. Det er ogs\xE5 de steder,
    hvor der er mest bambus, s\xE5 her m\xF8des dyrenes behov og menneskers behov.
    Det kan lade sig g\xF8re at dele plads, hvis nogle omr\xE5der beskyttes, og skoven
    forbliver sammenh\xE6ngende, men det kr\xE6ver, at man planl\xE6gger for det.\n\nN\xE5r
    du g\xE5r i zoo st\xF8tter du pandaerne, de er med i et avls program af China
    Wildlife Conservation Association som er del i at sikre pandaens langsigtede
    overlevelse. Hvis du skal k\xF8be bambus produkter kan du selv kigge efter FSC-m\xE6rkede
    produkter som garantere at vigtige levesteder ikke er blevet \xF8delagt. "
  titleEN: Staying In The Valley
  descriptionEN: 'The panda stays in the valley, where the forrest and the village
    meets. There is bamboo and water enough to get by, but there is also, noise,
    trafik and humans near by. Every new disturbance, makes it more difficult to
    find peace.


    In the valley humans and vild animals compete for the space.
    It is also these places where there is the most bamboo, so the animals and the
    humans needs meet here. It is possible to share the space, if some areas are
    protected, and the forest stays connected, but it reqires that is is palaned
    for.


    When you go to the zoo you are supporting the pandas, as they are
    a part of a breeding program for CHina Wildlife Conservation Association which
    ensures the pandas longterm survival. If you have to buy bamboo products, then
    you can look for FSC-labled products which gaurentee that important habitats
    do not get destroyed. '
  endingImage: {fileID: 0}
  endingDescription: 
